  "pluginId": 1579,
  "presentation": {
    "images": [],
    "plugin": {
      "description": "Computes the raw-material shopping list for FFXIV's daily Grand Company Supply and Provisioning missions. Reads today's 11 turn-ins (3 gatherers + 8 crafters), recursively expands each required item through the Lumina Recipe sheet down to gathered / vendor / drop leaves, and surfaces both a per-mission breakdown and a single aggregate list that calls out materials needed by multiple classes.\n\nv0.1.2 adds a \"Plan route on web\" button that hands the aggregate off to a companion route-planner page.\n\nv0.1.4 adds a \"Have\" column showing how many of each material are already in your bags / crystal pouch / saddlebag (HQ + NQ summed), with the same counts exported to the web page as the starting value of its editable progress column.\n\nPopulates the moment you open the Grand Company Personnel Officer's Supply / Provisioning list once per session.\n\nUsage:\n  /gcs    - open / close the main window",
      "images": [],
      "nsfw": false,
      "official": false,
      "richCard": false,
      "richnessScore": 1897,
      "summary": "Today's shopping list for all 11 Grand Company daily turn-ins.",
      "webEnriched": true
    },
    "projectRepository": "https://github.com/jdw-ss/gaming-tools",
    "schema": "omega.evidence.presentation.v1",
    "website": {
      "description": "Personal gaming-tools monorepo. Currently hosts the BulkDesynth Dalamud plugin (FFXIV).",
      "homepage": "",
      "images": [],
      "links": [
        {
          "kind": "source",
          "label": "Source",
          "url": "https://github.com/jdw-ss/gaming-tools"
        }
      ],
      "omegaBannerUrl": "",
      "readmeExcerpt": "# gaming-tools\n\nMonorepo for personal game tooling. Currently houses Dalamud (FFXIV) plugins\nunder [`FF14/`](./FF14). Each plugin builds and publishes independently via\nGitHub Actions; the resulting `pluginmaster.json` files are served from\nGitHub Pages so they can be subscribed to from inside the game client.\n\n## Plugins\n\n| Plugin | Path | Subscribe URL |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [Bulk Desynth](./FF14/BulkDesynth) | `FF14/BulkDesynth` | `https://jdw-ss.github.io/gaming-tools/ff14/bulkdesynth/pluginmaster.json` |\n| [Wondrous Tails Odds](./FF14/WondrousTailsSolver) | `FF14/WondrousTailsSolver` | `https://jdw-ss.github.io/gaming-tools/ff14/wondroustailssolver/pluginmaster.json` |\n| [GC Supply Helper](./FF14/GcSupplyHelper) | `FF14/GcSupplyHelper` | `https://jdw-ss.github.io/gaming-tools/ff14/gcsupplyhelper/pluginmaster.json` |\n\n(The subscribe URL works once the GitHub Pages site has been enabled on\nthis repository and the build workflow has run at least once — see\n[Deployment](#deployment) below.)\n\n## Layout\n\n```\n.\n├── .github/workflows/\n│   ├── build-bulkdesynth.yml          CI: build + publish BulkDesynth on push\n│   ├── build-wondroustailssolver.yml  CI: build + publish WondrousTailsOdds on push\n│   └── build-gcsupplyhelper.yml       CI: build + publish GcSupplyHelper on push\n├── docs/                              Output: served by GitHub Pages\n│   ├── ff14/bulkdesynth/\n│   │   ├── latest.zip\n│   │   └── pluginmaster.json\n│   ├── ff14/wondroustailssolver/\n│   │   ├── latest.zip\n│   │   └── pluginmaster.json\n│   └── ff14/gcsupplyhelper/\n│       ├── latest.zip\n│       └── pluginmaster.json\n└── FF14/\n    ├── BulkDesynth/                   Source for the BulkDesynth plugin\n    ├── WondrousTailsSolver/           Source for the WondrousTailsOdds plugin\n    └── GcSupplyHelper/                Source for the GcSupplyHelper plugin\n```\n\nThe `docs/` folder is the GitHub Pages root. Each plugin gets a dedicated\nsubpath so future plugins (e.g. `FF14/SomethingElse`) drop in without\ndisturbing existing subscribers.\n\n## Deployment\n\n1. Push the repo to GitHub (`gh repo create jdw-ss/gaming-tools --public --source=. --remote=origin`).\n2. On the repository's **Settings → Pages**, set:\n   - Source: *Deploy from a branch*\n   - Branch: `main` / folder: `/docs`\n3. Push any change under `FF14/BulkDesynth/**` (or trigger the workflow\n   manually). CI will build, zip, refresh `pluginmaster.json`, and commit\n   the new artifacts into `docs/ff14/bulkdesynth/` on `main`.\n4. In-game: Dalamud → Settings → Experimental → **Custom Plugin\n   Repositories** → paste the subscribe URL from the table above → Save.\n\nThe first build can take a couple of minutes (Pages needs to publish);\nsubsequent updates are picked up by Dalamud the next time it refreshes\nthe repo (or click the refresh icon on the row).\n\n## Per-plugin docs\n\nSee each plugin's own README for usage / commands / safety model:\n\n- [`FF14/BulkDesynth/README.md`](./FF14/BulkDesynth/README.md)\n- [`FF14/WondrousTailsSolver/README.md`](./FF14/WondrousTailsSolver/README.md)\n- [`FF14/GcSupplyHelper/README.md`](./FF14/GcSupplyHelper/README.md)",
      "title": "gaming-tools",
      "url": "https://github.com/jdw-ss/gaming-tools"
    }
  },
